<h1>Privacy</h1>

<p class="lede">This site does not ask who you are, does not use accounts and does not set cookies.</p>

<h2 id="tools">What you enter in the calculators</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Everything you enter is worked out in your own browser.</li>
  <li>Apart from the page address described below, the site does not send it to us or to anyone else, and does not save it.</li>
  <li>The history explorer puts its settings in the page address when you show a result, so that a copied link shows the same result. Like any page address, it is sent to the web host when the page loads, and your browser keeps it in its history.{% if site.analyticsToken %} The analytics service also sees it: see <a href="#analytics">Analytics</a>.{% endif %}</li>
  <li>The rule comparison and the triple lock calculator put nothing in the page address on their own. Each has a button, "Copy a link to this result", which copies a link holding the settings shown: what you chose and typed in the form, including any amount you entered, so do not share the link if an amount is your own. Opening such a link shows that result. Like any page address, it is then sent to the web host when the page loads, and your browser keeps it in its history.{% if site.analyticsToken %} The analytics service also sees it: see <a href="#analytics">Analytics</a>.{% endif %} If the link cannot be copied, the page puts it in the address bar for you to copy from there.</li>
  <li>The budget explorer puts nothing in the page address, and the site keeps nothing you enter in it. If your browser brings the budget explorer back when you return to it, the page clears your amounts and the result. A browser can still offer to fill in a form from its own memory. That is a browser setting, not this site.</li>
  <li>The budget explorer has a button, "Clear everything I entered", that clears it at once.</li>
</ul>
<p>If you download or copy a table from the history explorer, the file holds the rates shown and any calculation you chose to add. It holds nothing about you.</p>

<h2 id="analytics">Analytics</h2>
{% if site.analyticsToken %}
<p>This site uses <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a> to count visits. Your browser fetches its counting script from Cloudflare, so Cloudflare receives the technical details of that request, as a web host does. Cloudflare says the service records aggregate information, such as how many people viewed a page and which site they came from, sets no cookies, stores nothing on your device and builds no profile of you. It also says it does not record the part of a page address after a question mark, which is where the history explorer keeps its settings as you use it, and where a link copied from the rule comparison or the triple lock calculator carries the settings shown, including any amount typed into them. The budget explorer puts nothing in the address. Read the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>.</p>
{% else %}
<p>This preview has no analytics and loads nothing from any other website. The published site uses Cloudflare Web Analytics, and this page then says what is collected. Amounts entered in the budget explorer are never in the page address; an amount entered in the rule comparison or the triple lock calculator is in a link only if you copy one.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2 id="hosting">The company that hosts the site</h2>
<p>Any web host keeps a technical record of requests, such as the address of the page asked for and the time. This site is hosted by Netlify. Read the <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/">Netlify privacy notice</a>.</p>

<h2 id="links">Links to other websites</h2>
<p>This site links to GOV.UK, to the publishers of its sources and to its two sister sites. Each has its own privacy notice.</p>
